<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Dynamic Guidance with DDPM</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Extending Dynamic Guidance to DDPM is straightforward. We describe the algorithm in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ A.1 Dynamic Guidance with DDPM ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. In the main paper we employed DDIM as it is the more practical for sampling from models with complexity larger than the toy 2D Gaussian setting.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Dynamic Guidance with DDPM</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_align_center ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> timesteps <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, dynamic guidance steps <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoiser <math id="alg2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, classifier <math id="alg2.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T\dots 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T\dots 1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{1}\geq t\geq T_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{1}\geq t\geq T_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{*}=\argmax p_{\phi}(y|{\bm{x}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{*}=\argmax p_{\phi}(y|{\bm{x}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-1}=\mu_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t},t)+\sigma_{t}^{2}\lambda\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}p_{\phi}(y^{*}|{\bm{x}}_{t})+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-1}=\mu_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t},t)+\sigma_{t}^{2}\lambda\nabla_{{\bm{x}}_{t}}p_{\phi}(y^{*}|{\bm{x}}_{t})+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>


</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-1}=\mu_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t},t)+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐳</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-1}=\mu_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t},t)+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{z}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg2.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Additional Metrics</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also compute Inception and CLIP FID and observe that, in most settings, Dynamic Guidance outperforms Classifier Guidance. For high guidance scales (<math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=10</annotation></semantics></math>) Dynamic Guidance is biased towards generating classes that are better aligned with the initial noise. Thus, when generating, we end up with samples that are not distributed uniform across the ImageNet classes. We demonstrate this observation in Figures <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure A.5 ‣ A.2 Additional Metrics ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.5</span></a> and <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure A.6 ‣ A.2 Additional Metrics ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.6</span></a>, where we show the final classification label for the generated images using Classifier Guidance and Dynamic Guidance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By not generating all classes equally, the Inception FID is affected since the Inception model is heavily biased towards balanced ImageNet generation (trained on ImageNet-1k), On the other hand, the performance of CLIP FID is not as heavily affected. To perform a fair comparison between Dynamic Guidance and Classifier Guidance that strictly enforces a balanced generated distribution for evaluation, we generate 100k samples and perform stratified sampling on the generated set to approximate a balanced 10k-sample distribution. We report the results in Table <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ A.2 Additional Metrics ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> in the row titled <em id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">+ DG <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=10</annotation></semantics></math> (balanced)</em>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Inception and CLIP FID on ImageNet.</figcaption>
