<th id="A1.T6.2.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">+ DG <math id="A1.T6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=20</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T6.2.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">25.58</td>
<td id="A1.T6.2.11.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">37.07</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05356v1/gen_classes_scale_1.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:411/366;" width="411" height="366" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.5: </span>Distribution of final predicted ImageNet classes for samples generated with Classifier and Dynamic guidance using <math id="A1.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05356v1/gen_classes_scale_10.png" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:411/364;" width="411" height="364" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.6: </span>Distribution of final predicted ImageNet classes for samples generated with Classifier and Dynamic guidance using <math id="A1.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span><math id="A1.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE Implementation</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the Single Shapes dataset, we want to examine the score function across latent directions where interpolation would lead to hallucinations. To do that, we first train a <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Higgins et al., 2017</a>)</cite>; a variational autoencoder that produces interpretable, disentangled latent representations of the images. We train the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE with a latent dimension of 10 and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=4</annotation></semantics></math> for 500 epochs and a batch size of 4096 using an unofficial PyTorch re-implementation<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            https://github.com/1Konny/Beta-VAE</span></span></span> on a mix of images from both the Single Shapes and the Mixed Shapes datasets. This is crucial so that the VAE can learn the representation of both real and hallucinated samples for each of those datasets. Using the VAE, we find that specific latent dimensions learned by the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE alter the image in distinct, orthogonal ways, which we show in Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure A.7 ‣ A.3 𝛽-VAE Implementation ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a>. As described in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Score Function Sharpening ‣ 4 Dynamic Guidance ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>, we can then use the learned decomposition of the images learned by the VAE and visualize the score function in its latent space.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05356v1/latent_traversal.png" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/172;" width="548" height="172" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.7: </span>Change in different latent dimensions learned by the <math id="A1.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE alter the image in distinct ways; latent dimension 9 controls the appearance of the shape on the left, latent dimension 0 controls the appearance of the shape on the right, and latent dimension 0 controls the position of the shape on the right.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Difference in guidance norms </h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Figures <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure A.8 ‣ A.4 Difference in guidance norms ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a> and <a href="#A1.F9" title="Figure A.9 ‣ A.4 Difference in guidance norms ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.9</span></a> we generate images from the same initial noise using classifier guidance and dynamic guidance and compare the norms guidance gradient. We find that the ’static’ classifier guidance often fails to sufficiently align the generated image with the target class, which translates to the gradient norm being large during the end of the denoising process. We hypothesize that this ’mismatch’ between noise and class is one of the reasons leading to the model generating hallucinations. While the initial noise dictates a specific structure in the generated image, the assigned initial class does not align with that structure, leading to unwanted interpolation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05356v1/norms_llama.png" id="A1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:548/744;" width="548" height="744" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.8: </span>Generated samples from ImageNet using Classifier Guidance with a fixed label and Dynamic Guidance. In classifier guided samples the norm of the denoising step gets bigger towards the end of sampling, meaning that the required denoising steps become significantly larger.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05356v1/norm_random.png" id="A1.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:548/747;" width="548" height="747" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.9: </span>Generated samples from ImageNet using Classifier Guidance with a random label and Dynamic Guidance. In classifier guided samples the norm of the denoising step gets bigger towards the end of sampling, meaning that the required denoising steps become significantly larger.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Additional Figures</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we provide additional Figures and qualitative examples:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure A.7 ‣ A.3 𝛽-VAE Implementation ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.7</span></a> shows that change in different latent dimensions learned by the <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>-VAE alter the image in distinct; controlled ways.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure A.10 ‣ A.5 Additional Figures ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.10</span></a> shows how Dynamic Guidance fixes a sample that would end up being a hallucination during sampling.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A1.F11" title="Figure A.11 ‣ A.5 Additional Figures ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a> and <a href="#A1.F12" title="Figure A.12 ‣ A.5 Additional Figures ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.12</span></a> show 100 images of hands generated with DDIM and Dynamic Guidance respectively.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A1.F14" title="Figure A.14 ‣ A.5 Additional Figures ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.14</span></a>, <a href="#A1.F14" title="Figure A.14 ‣ A.5 Additional Figures ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.14</span></a>, <a href="#A1.F16" title="Figure A.16 ‣ A.5 Additional Figures ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.16</span></a> and <a href="#A1.F16" title="Figure A.16 ‣ A.5 Additional Figures ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Mitigating Diffusion Model Hallucinations with Dynamic Guidance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.16</span></a> show examples of random images generated images with Classifier or Dynamic Guidance with different guidance scales.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05356v1/figures/sampling.png" id="A1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/549;" width="548" height="549" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.10: </span><math id="A1.F10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{{\bm{x}}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> during sampling with Dynamic Guidance using initial noise <math id="A1.F10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> that would result in a hallucination. We see that Dynamic Guidance guides the model to generate the thumb that would otherwise be missing and results in a sample with correct anatomy.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05356v1/hands_qual_ddim.png" id="A1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/548;" width="548" height="548" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.11: </span>Generated samples from the hands dataset using DDIM. Hallucinations in red.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05356v1/hands_qual_dmlcg.png" id="A1.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:548/548;" width="548" height="548" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.12: </span>Generated samples from the hands dataset using Dynamic Guidance. Hallucinations in red.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F14" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.05356v1/cg_scale_1.png" id="A1.F14.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:384/384;" width="384" height="384" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.13: </span>Random ImageNet samples generated with Classifier Guidance using <math id="A1.F14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.05356v1/dg_scale_1.png" id="A1.F14.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:384/384;" width="384" height="384" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.14: </span>Random ImageNet samples generated with Dynamic Guidance using <math id="A1.F14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F16" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.05356v1/cg_scale_10.png" id="A1.F16.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:384/385;" width="384" height="385" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.15: </span>Random ImageNet samples generated with Classifier Guidance using <math id="A1.F16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2510.05356v1/dg_scale_10.png" id="A1.F16.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:384/385;" width="384" height="385" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure A.16: </span>Random ImageNet samples generated with Dynamic Guidance using <math id="A1.F16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=10</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
